{
  "$comment": "Mask Composite's quote before a run, read by BOTH estimates over the same graphs: the editor's (frontend maskCompositePricingUnits — the node's pill, its Run button, the confirm and the workflow badge) and the server's run estimate (CreditsService.estimateWorkflowBaseCredits). Each case wires its sources into the composite `c`; `expectedUnits` is the 5-second units both quote (60 = the 300 s cap). The sources here are uploads, Library clips and Video links (recordings, read the same way by both through the shared measured walk, `measuredWireLengthSec`); a video another node makes — a generation, an Extend Video, a step that re-runs, and a chain built on one — is held to the same parity by the sibling fixture planned-length-quote-parity.json, for Mask Composite and Video Overlay both. `fallbackDecidedBefore` marks a shape the editor used to price from a length the upstream node merely stores (an upload's metadata, a Video link's whole length) — the server never read it, so the editor now quotes the cap there too. `libraryAsset` is the Library asset a case's upload node was added from: the editor half builds that node through `assetToUploadNode` and holds it to `nodes[0].data` (all but the row's `jobId` and `timestamp`, which no reader reads), so the server half reads exactly what a Library add writes.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an uploaded clip: the result row the upload recorded for its current file",
      "composite": {},
      "nodes": [
        { "id": "u", "type": "upload-video", "data": { "url": "https://cdn.example/clip.mp4", "metadata": { "durationSeconds": 23 }, "generatedResults": [{ "url": "https://cdn.example/clip.mp4", "duration": 23 }], "activeResultIndex": 0 } }
      ],
      "edges": [{ "source": "u", "targetHandle": "video" }],
      "expectedUnits": 5
    },
    {
      "name": "an upload that declares its length with the node (an API-written workflow)",
      "composite": {},
      "nodes": [
        { "id": "u", "type": "upload-video", "data": { "url": "https://cdn.example/clip.mp4", "duration": 12 } }
      ],
      "edges": [{ "source": "u", "targetHandle": "video" }],
      "expectedUnits": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "pixelate: the background's recorded length, never the foreground's",
      "composite": { "fill": "pixelate" },
      "nodes": [
        { "id": "f", "type": "upload-video", "data": { "url": "https://cdn.example/f.mp4", "duration": 12 } },
        { "id": "b", "type": "upload-video", "data": { "url": "https://cdn.example/b.mp4", "duration": 41 } }
      ],
      "edges": [{ "source": "f", "targetHandle": "video" }, { "source": "b", "targetHandle": "background-video" }],
      "expectedUnits": 9
    },
    {
      "name": "nothing wired: the cap",
      "composite": {},
      "nodes": [],
